-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, so no compensation is owed.\n\nTHE RIDER'S ARGUMENTS. The POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 claims are accepted. The separate POL-NS-04 'exoneration' argument is rejected on its own terms: limb (a) requires a rider message that is locating or coordinating — an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that the vehicle cannot be seen. The rider's only message is 'ok' (EV-CHAT-02744, sent 08:13:05); it is none of those, so limb (a) fails and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate. The refund is unaffected because it follows from the driver's own evidence under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06.\n\nCOMPENSATION. No driver compensation and no goodwill. POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 in full. POL-NS-03's pin-ambiguity goodwill (50% of the fee) fires only where neither party named a sub-location AND trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 2 or more; the record shows 1 registered pickup point and neither chat message names a sub-location, so neither limb (i) nor limb (ii) of POL-NS-03 applies.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHT. EV-ADVIS-02744-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and can carry no fact; it carries no deciding fact here (the dwell falls short of the minimum on its own), and its absence merely makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, which changes nothing since there are no in-geofence intervals to sum. The deciding facts rest on EV-GPS-02744, EV-TRIP-02744 and EV-FARE-02744, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the 0.70 floor and is 0.90. The two claims asserting the missing advisory (one from each side) were discarded by the referee for non-disclosure of its impairment and are not relied on.\n\nEXECUTION. A refund of SGD 4.50 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes automatically on issue. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04.",
